    "body": "You've been waiting for it all year, and now the Black Friday sales are finally here. It's that time of the year when your favorite 3D printer makers roll out huge discounts on some of their best products, and you can be sure that we will be here tracking them all for you live. So whether you are a new maker searching for an affordable, easy-to-use 3D printer to get you started, or a serious hobbyist looking to upgrade your workshop or expand your print farm, there is no better time to dive in and get the best bang for your buck than today. Throughout our live coverage, we will be rounding up the best deals from top 3D printer brands such as Bambu Lab, Prusa, Creality, Elegoo, Anycubic, Snapmaker, and more. From FDM and resin printers to tool changers and multicolor machines, we've got you covered. We'll also be keeping an eye out for savings on filaments and resin, as well as discounts on all those handy maker tools and 3D printer accessories. We're backing up our deal selections with in-depth reviews, benchmarks, and comprehensive historical pricing analysis. We're checking deals around the clock to find the best options and keep this page up to date, but please note that they often won't last long, so you'll need to act quickly. So sit back, relax, and let us do all the grunt work for you. Be sure to check back often, as we'll be keeping tabs on all the Black Friday sales as they unfold, and you're not going to want to miss out! Amazon: All Black Friday 3D Printer Deals Amazon: Black Friday Filament Discounts Amazon: Bambu Lab P2S Combo now $649.99 (was $769) * The listed previous prices can vary based on retailer, as many use different metrics, like 90-day rolling averages or ‘estimated value’ due to ongoing shortages and price hikes. Snapmaker’s U1 kicked off the affordable tool changer craze around this time last year, with an early Kickstarter price of $799 and a full retail price of $999. But now it’s widely available and on sale for $100 less than ever. When we reviewed the U1, we praised its roomy build area (270 mm cubed), direct-drive tool heads, and its four-head tool-changing capabilities, earning it 4.5 stars and a spot on our best 3D printers list. On the heels of the U1, Flashforge released the Creator 5, a tool changer that’s a bit more basic, but still a solid machine (we gave it 4 stars in our review), priced even lower than the Snapmaker, both when it launched (at $699) and now, when it’s on sale for $100 less. — Matt Safford Creality's K2 Combo is the smallest in the K2 family, with a print area of 260 x 260 x 260mm. Direct from Creality, you can save $200 on the printer itself, bringing its $549 list price down to $349 for Black Friday. Bundled with a Creality CFS quadruple-spool feeder, you'll also save $200 off the $699 list price, bringing the price down to $499. As with our K2 printers, such as the K2 Pro Combo we reviewed, you can pair up to four CFS cartridges together for a 16-color printer; though, with the smaller size here, it might be difficult to fit all those colors in. It also features auto print bed leveling, along with print failure detection. — Jake Roach",
